//RS /// An embedder holding a checked bundle reaches the JIT without ever touching
//RS /// the driver's compile entries, so the Cranelift backend has to own the same
//RS /// sized stack they own: MIR lowering and the whole-program interpreter on the
//RS /// deopt route are the same unbounded-depth recursive descent, and either tier
//RS /// alone exhausts a 2 MiB embedder thread.
